From 0dfc83f9af04b133696a7167f93e50b8d6932601 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: VCKing101 <59761021+VCKing101@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 09:29:47 +1030
Subject: [PATCH 27/39] Interface: pictures of the port's own over the running
 game

A port that extends one of the game's screens needs to show it there: a
hint beside a menu, a highlight round a box the port gives new controls.
The only picture a program around the port could draw over the game was
set_status_overlay, one line for the desktop app.

- ui::add_game_overlay(visible, draw): asked before every game frame;
  `draw` builds its part of the frame with Dear ImGui, under the menu.
  The game's dialogs, when open, are drawn instead, as before. Several may
  be added.
- ui::game_picture(): where the game's 480x272 picture was last drawn, in
  ImGui's (window) coordinates, from the renderer's last blit
  (VulkanRenderer::game_picture), so a point of the PSP's screen can be
  found in any window size, aspect setting or display scale.
- ui::game_text_font(): the face the game's own text is drawn with
  (fonts::active_face, the menu's Font setting when the interface starts),
  loaded as an ImGui font, so text beside the game's matches it.

Nothing is drawn until a port adds an overlay.

Verified: the Dissidia 012 port draws its BGM focus outline, series line
and hints with it on the recompiled build (Windows, 960x544 window); the
captures show them at the game box's place and in the game's font.
Not verified: other games, fullscreen and the Fill aspect, Android, a font
changed in the menu after start (the overlay keeps the first one).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
